claim.claim-text:
selecting content that is age appropriate for a particular infant;
altering a sound emission of a recording of a care-giver of the particular infant reciting the content to have age appropriate audio parameters to generate the audio output; and
programming the audio device (10, 110) to emit the audio output below an age dependent volume, for an age dependent number of intervals per day and per week, for an age dependent duration.

approximately 55dB for infants that are postmenstrual age of 28 to 40 weeks;
approximately 65db for infants that are 0-3 months old;
approximately 75db for infants that are 3-6 months old; and
approximately 85db for infants that are 6-12 months old.

3-4 times per week for infants that are postmenstrual age of 28 to 32 weeks with not more than 20 minutes of total audio output per day;
equal to or less than 6 times per day for infants that are postmenstrual age of 32 to 36 weeks with not more than 3 hours of total audio output per day with at least 30 minutes of silence between each interval;
equal to or less than 8 times per day for infants that are postmenstrual age of 36 to 40 weeks and 0-3 months with not more than 4 hours of total audio output per day with at least 30 minutes of silence between each interval; and
an unlimited number of times per day for infants that are over 3 months old with at least 30 minutes of silence between each interval.

approximately 20 minutes for infants that are postmenstrual age of 32 to 36 weeks;
approximately 30 minutes for infants that are postmenstrual age of 36 to 40 weeks;
approximately 30 minutes for infants that are 0-6 months old; and
approximately 45 minutes for infants that are 6-12 months old.

a song having less than 3 chords, a single octave range, a single accapella voice, sung at a tempo of less than 60 beats per minute (BPM) and a stepwise melody with no intervals greater than a third for infants that are postmenstrual age of 28 to 32 weeks;
a song having less than 4 chords, an octave range 1.5 octaves, a single voice with a single instrument playing single notes, sung at a tempo of less than 60 BPM and a stepwise melody with no intervals greater than a sixth for infants that are postmenstrual age of 32 to 40 weeks;
a song having unlimited chords, an unlimited octave range, a single voice with a single instrument playing single and multiple notes, sung at a tempo of less than 120 BPM and any melody for infants that are between 0 to 3 months;
a song having unlimited chords, an unlimited octave range, 4 voices or less with 4 instruments or less playing single and multiple notes, sung at a tempo of less than 120 BPM and any melody for infants that are between 3 to 6 months; and
a song having unlimited chords, an unlimited octave range, unlimited voices with unlimited instruments playing single and multiple notes, sung at a tempo of less than 120 BPM and any melody for infants that are between 6 to 12 months.

a speaker (38) configured to emit audio;
an electrical circuit to convert an audio signal received by input to the electrical circuit into an audio input for the speaker (38);
a microcomputer (32) in communication with the speaker (38); and
a battery (30) to power at least one of the electronic components.
